\cf0 The sculptural installation of 
\f0\i Damaged Goods
\f1\i0  is inspired by the seminal 1986 "Damaged Goods" exhibition at the New Museum in New York, which focused on artworks that addressed consumer culture. In searching curator Brian Wallis' exhibition catalog online, I discovered a preponderance of 
\f0\i other 
\f1\i0 books sharing the same title as his; these ranged from romance novels to self-help books to memoirs. Invariably the books\'92 cover designs featured a woman as the eponymous damaged good.\'a0The shelf above displays a selected of 13 of these books from my ever-expanding collection.\
